    {
      "id": "matter",
      "en": "Matter",
      "note": "Load-bearing term (the client-engagement workspace); must not drift into synonyms. The internal `workspace` alias means the same thing where user-facing (createNewWorkspace = \"Create new matter\"); render it with the Matter term, not a literal \"workspace\" translation. ar uses ملف قانوني (legal file/dossier): bare ملف is also the everyday word for a computer file, so labels, pickers, and scope options rendered with it collided with Files; the qualifier carries the concept, and the short form stays only where the sentence already names the matter. Avoid قضية (lawsuit) and مسألة (abstract legal question). cs \"případ\" / sk \"prípad\" are banned in the nominative singular and plural only: those are the forms a label or term takes (a landing nav label had drifted to \"Případy\"), while the oblique forms carry the everyday idiom \"v případě\" (\"in case of\") and would false-fire.",
